lls and was represented at the 2004 edition by Burcică and her partner from the 2000 Games, " [:a {:href ""} "Angela Alupei"] ". Romania had not been as dominant at the World Championships, however, having won bronze in 2001 and 2003 with different crews, as Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/92576"} "Claudia Blasberg"] " had won the 2001 and 2003 titles, as well as silver in 2002 and at the 2000 Olympics. In Athens, Blasberg was partnered with " [:a {:href "/athletes/104202"} "Daniela Reimer"] ". Romania won its heat in the opening round in Olympic record time, but this record was quickly broken by Australians " [:a {:href "/athletes/35330"} "Sally Newmarch"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/104210"} "Amber Halliday"] " , the latter of whom was the 2002 World Champion and 2003 runner-up. Germany, meanwhile, took the other heat. In the semi-finals, Romania and Australia were victorious in their heats, while Germany avoided elimination by a margin of less than a second. In the final, however, the first four finishers, Romania, Germany, the Dutch duo of " [:a {:href "/athletes/92642"} "Kirsten van der Kolk"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/92646"} "Marit van Eupen"] ", and Australia were all spaced out by at least one second in that order."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/39484"} "Constanţa Burcică"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/39532"} "Angela Alupei"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ROU"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ROU.png"}] "ROU"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/104202"} "Daniela Reimer"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/92576"} "Claudia Blasberg"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GER"} [:img {:style "